  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25g-perchlike-fishes-7-remaining-groups/only-in-the-transit/",
      "html": "<p>The Rainbow Darter (Etheostoma caeruleum) is a pretty, small species that attains a maximum length of 7-8 cm. It has been imported since as early as 1899, but it has always stayed rare.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25g-perchlike-fishes-7-remaining-groups/only-in-the-transit/",
      "html": "<p>There are not many species of fish in which the demand is greater than the number of offered animals. The Rainbow Darter belongs to these exceptional species.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25g-perchlike-fishes-7-remaining-groups/only-in-the-transit/",
      "html": "<p>The species comes from North America.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25g-perchlike-fishes-7-remaining-groups/only-in-the-transit/",
      "html": "<p>In the wild the Rainbow Darter inhabits cool, fast running water.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25g-perchlike-fishes-7-remaining-groups/only-in-the-transit/",
      "html": "<p>The species deposits the eggs in the ground.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25g-perchlike-fishes-7-remaining-groups/only-in-the-transit/",
      "html": "<p>Although it inhabits cool, fast running water in the wild, it is all but demanding.</p>"
    }
  ],
